        "document": {
          "text": "Orion V500 and Birch B200 were tested in the same room. The first television had its brightness measured in HDR mode. The second television used SDR settings with a different white point. The reviewing team logged both protocols separately.\n\nThis TV looked brighter in a scene that contained very small highlights. However, the reviewer did not identify which model was connected during the second viewing. The colorimeter was calibrated before the test.\n\nNeither observation establishes a superiority claim across the two models.",
          "sha256": "ccb5f90b533cdfc7c7e2fb0baa3d23945cebfd8fb442415e49ee59e503ea6d88",
          "source": {
